# SwiftFormat configuration for VaderCleaner.
#
# Deliberately minimal. The codebase is already hand-formatted consistently
# (4-space indent throughout, no tab-indented files, every file ends in a
# newline), and its own guidance prefers consistency within a file over a global
# standard. A full SwiftFormat run would rewrite all 250 files and bury real
# changes in reformatting noise.
#
# So this enables only the rules that enforce invariants the code already holds
# to — running it is a near no-op today (8 trailing-whitespace lines) and it
# stays that way. Formatting judgment stays with the author.

--swiftversion 6.0

# Allowlist: only these rules run. Everything else is disabled by omission.
--rules trailingSpace,linebreakAtEndOfFile,consecutiveBlankLines,consecutiveSpaces,duplicateImports,blankLinesAtStartOfScope,blankLinesAtEndOfScope,todos

--maxwidth none
--trimwhitespace always

--exclude .build,DerivedData,Vendor,.claude,Scripts
